## Night level 1 — hedgehog: loc_brush_pile, loc_flowerpots, loc_mushrooms

animal-hedgehog = Hedgehog
animal-hedgehog-more = More about the hedgehog

# kiga: shown next to a picture (hedgehog spines)
mission-hedgehog-facts-kiga = spines
mission-hedgehog-facts-klasse1 = I have lots of spines. I curl up tight. I am awake at night.
mission-hedgehog-facts-klasse2 = Hedgehogs have up to 8,000 spines on their backs. When they are scared, they roll up tight so that only their spines show. They sleep during the day and look for food at night. They like to eat beetles and worms.
mission-hedgehog-facts-klasse3 = A hedgehog has up to 8,000 spines. They are special hairs that are hollow inside but still very strong. With its fine nose it finds beetles, worms and snails at night. In winter the hedgehog hibernates and only wakes up again in spring. When it looks for food, it snuffles and smacks its lips so loudly that you can hear it.

# loc_brush_pile — heap of dry twigs and sticks in the corner where two hedges meet; rustling (kiga picture: heap of dry twigs in the hedge corner)
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_brush_pile-kiga = twigs
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_brush_pile-klasse1 = I am small and spiky. I sleep under dry sticks. It rustles softly.
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_brush_pile-klasse2 = The hedgehog is hiding in the corner by the hedge, under a heap of dry sticks. Listen closely: something rustles there softly.
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_brush_pile-klasse3 = Hedgehogs sleep during the day and only wake up at night. Our hedgehog has built a cosy hiding spot: far back in the corner where two hedges meet. A big heap of dry sticks and branches lies there. When the hedgehog moves, it cracks and rustles softly.

# loc_flowerpots — potting bench with stacked clay flowerpots, white night-scented flowers (sweet smell at night) (kiga picture: old clay flowerpots on and under a potting bench, white flowers)
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_flowerpots-kiga = flowerpots
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_flowerpots-klasse1 = I like to sniff. It smells sweet here. White flowers bloom at night.
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_flowerpots-klasse2 = The hedgehog is sniffing at old clay pots. White flowers grow in them that only smell so sweet at night.
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_flowerpots-klasse3 = During the day you can hardly smell anything here. But when it gets dark, little white flowers open and smell sweet. They grow in old clay pots that stand on and under a wooden table. Our hedgehog is sniffing between the pots with its little nose.

# loc_mushrooms — ring of brown/cream mushrooms on moss at the foot of a big old tree; earthy smell (kiga picture: ring of brown mushrooms on green moss under a big old tree)
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_mushrooms-kiga = mushrooms
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_mushrooms-klasse1 = The ground is soft. It smells of damp earth. Green moss grows here.
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_mushrooms-klasse2 = The hedgehog sits on soft green moss under a thick old tree. Little brown caps stand in a circle around it, and it smells of damp earth.
mission-hedgehog-riddle-loc_mushrooms-klasse3 = Under a big old tree the ground is as soft as a pillow. Green moss grows there, and it smells of damp earth and old wood. Little brown and pale caps stand in a circle like a ring. Our hedgehog has curled up right in the middle of this ring.

mission-hedgehog-home = Great! The hedgehogs are home again.

## Night level 1 — bat: loc_windmill, loc_fireflies, loc_hollow_tree

animal-bat = Bat
animal-bat-more = More about the bat

# kiga: shown next to a picture (bat with open wings)
mission-bat-facts-kiga = wings
mission-bat-facts-klasse1 = I can fly. I hang upside down. I like to eat fruit.
mission-bat-facts-klasse2 = Bats are the only mammals that can really fly. Their wings are made of thin skin between long fingers. Our bat is a fruit bat and loves to eat sweet fruit.
mission-bat-facts-klasse3 = Bats sleep upside down during the day and hold on with the claws of their feet. At night they wake up and fly off. Fruit bats like ours have big eyes and a good nose, which help them find ripe fruit. To sleep, they wrap themselves in their wings like in a blanket.

# loc_windmill — little wooden garden windmill, four sails turning, soft whirring (kiga picture: little wooden windmill with four turning sails at night)
mission-bat-riddle-loc_windmill-kiga = windmill
mission-bat-riddle-loc_windmill-klasse1 = I hang upside down. Big sails turn round. It whirs softly.
mission-bat-riddle-loc_windmill-klasse2 = The bat hangs upside down under a small wooden house with four big sails turning in the wind. You can hear a soft whirring.
mission-bat-riddle-loc_windmill-klasse3 = Bats like to rest upside down. Our bat has found a place where something turns in the wind. Four big wooden sails go round and round, always in a circle. It whirs and creaks softly, and the bat sways gently along.

# loc_fireflies — low meadow with many fireflies (the only firefly place, Q-115), small crooked tree (kiga picture: short meadow full of glowing fireflies, small crooked tree)
mission-bat-riddle-loc_fireflies-kiga = fireflies
mission-bat-riddle-loc_fireflies-klasse1 = Little lights dance here. I hang from a branch. It twinkles everywhere.
mission-bat-riddle-loc_fireflies-klasse2 = The bat hangs from a small crooked tree. Lots of little yellow lights dance around it through the night.
mission-bat-riddle-loc_fireflies-klasse3 = Tonight one place in the garden glows in a very special way. Lots of tiny creatures fly around there, and each one has a little yellow light on its tummy. They blink and dance through the air. Right in the middle our bat hangs upside down from a crooked tree and watches the dance of lights.

# loc_hollow_tree — very thick old tree with a big round knothole at 2.5 m (kiga picture: very thick old tree with a big round knothole)
mission-bat-riddle-loc_hollow_tree-kiga = knothole
mission-bat-riddle-loc_hollow_tree-klasse1 = The tree is very thick. It has a round hole. I hang there.
mission-bat-riddle-loc_hollow_tree-klasse2 = The bat hangs on a very old, very thick tree. In its trunk there is a big round hole, like a little window.
mission-bat-riddle-loc_hollow_tree-klasse3 = This tree is the thickest and oldest in the whole garden. Three children together could hardly hug it. High up, its trunk has a big round hole, dark and cosy. Our bat hangs upside down right in front of it, holding on with its little claws.

mission-bat-home = Great! The bats are home again.

## Night level 1 — owl: loc_moon_pond, loc_hilltop, loc_fir

animal-owl = Owl
animal-owl-more = More about the owl

# kiga: shown next to a picture (owl face with big round eyes)
mission-owl-facts-kiga = eyes
mission-owl-facts-klasse1 = I have big eyes. I fly very quietly. I call: hoo-hoo!
mission-owl-facts-klasse2 = Owls see and hear very well at night. They can turn their heads far round to the back. Their soft feathers make almost no sound when they fly.
mission-owl-facts-klasse3 = Owls are night birds. With their big eyes they see much better in the dark than we do. They can turn their heads almost all the way to the back without moving their bodies. Because their feathers are so soft, they fly almost silently. Our owl likes to eat beetles best.

# loc_moon_pond — small still pond mirroring the moon and stars, reeds, owl on a wooden post at the shore (kiga picture: still pond at night with the moon and stars mirrored in it, reeds, a wooden post)
mission-owl-riddle-loc_moon_pond-kiga = pond
mission-owl-riddle-loc_moon_pond-klasse1 = The moon floats on water. I sit on a post. The reeds rustle.
mission-owl-riddle-loc_moon_pond-klasse2 = The owl sits on a wooden post by the water. Below it the stars glitter, and the moon seems to swim in the still water.
mission-owl-riddle-loc_moon_pond-klasse3 = When the air is completely still, the water becomes as smooth as a mirror. Then you can see the moon and lots of stars in it, as if the sky were lying on the ground. Reeds sway on the bank, and a small jetty leads out a little way. Our owl sits on a wooden post next to it and admires the moon.

# loc_hilltop — small grassy hill with a big round stone on top, no trees, brightest moonlight (kiga picture: small round grassy hill with a big round stone on top in bright moonlight)
mission-owl-riddle-loc_hilltop-kiga = hill
mission-owl-riddle-loc_hilltop-klasse1 = I sit at the top. No tree grows here. The moon shines brightly.
mission-owl-riddle-loc_hilltop-klasse2 = The owl sits on top of a big round stone. No trees stand there, so the moon shines brightest here.
mission-owl-riddle-loc_hilltop-klasse3 = Owls have big eyes and see very well in the dark. But tonight our owl likes it especially bright. It has flown to where the ground rises a little and no tree hides the moon. It sits right at the top on a big round stone in the silvery moonlight.

# loc_fir — the one tall dark pointed fir tree with cones (kiga picture: tall dark pointed fir tree with cones, owl at the very top)
mission-owl-riddle-loc_fir-kiga = fir
mission-owl-riddle-loc_fir-klasse1 = I sit very high. The tree is pointed. It has cones.
mission-owl-riddle-loc_fir-klasse2 = The owl sits at the very top of a tall, pointed tree with dark needles and cones. From up there it calls: hoo-hoo!
mission-owl-riddle-loc_fir-klasse3 = In the garden there is a tree that stays green even in winter. It has dark, sharp needles, and brown cones hang from its branches. Its top points into the sky like an arrow. Our owl sits right up on this top and softly calls: hoo-hoo!

mission-owl-home = Great! The owls are home again.

## Night flow (GAME-NIGHT)

# Nightfall, after the last day animal is home (GAME-NIGHT rule 1)
night-dusk-kiga = night
night-dusk-klasse1 = All animals are home. Night is falling.
night-dusk-klasse2 = All the animals are home again. Now it is getting dark, and the lanterns light up.
night-dusk-klasse3 = You did it! All the animals are home again. The sun goes down, the sky turns deep blue, and lanterns light up everywhere. Now you can go to bed or walk through the moon door into the night zoo.

# Reading panel at the bed (zookeeper house, NIGHT-003)
night-bed-kiga = bed
night-bed-klasse1 = You can sleep here. Good night!
night-bed-klasse2 = Are you tired? Lie down in the bed. The zoo will be waiting in the morning.
night-bed-klasse3 = The bed is soft and warm, and the moon shines through the window. If you lie down, you will sleep until the next morning. Your game is saved while you sleep.

# Reading panel at the moon door (level 1, GAME-NIGHT rule 3)
night-moon-door-kiga = moon door
night-moon-door-klasse1 = The moon door is open! Come along!
night-moon-door-klasse2 = The moon door is glowing. Behind it live animals that are awake at night.
night-moon-door-klasse3 = The night zoo lies behind the moon door. Animals live there that sleep during the day and are awake at night. But tonight they have run away too!

# First step into night_1 (cut-in)
night-welcome-kiga = night zoo
night-welcome-klasse1 = Welcome to the night zoo! Where are the animals?
night-welcome-klasse2 = Welcome to the night zoo! The hedgehog, the bat and the owl are gone. Read the boards at the night house.
night-welcome-klasse3 = Welcome to the night zoo! It is quiet here, only the crickets are chirping. The hedgehog, the bat and the owl have run away from the night house. Read the boards in front of the house and take your lantern: in its light the animals' eyes shine.

# All night_1 animals home (GAME-NIGHT rule 7)
night-complete-kiga = bed
night-complete-klasse1 = All night animals are home. Time for bed!
night-complete-klasse2 = Well done! All the night animals are home again. Now go to bed; tomorrow a new part of the zoo is waiting.
night-complete-klasse3 = Well done! The hedgehog, the bat and the owl are back in their house. It is late, and the stars are twinkling. Go back through the moon door and lie down in bed. Tomorrow morning a new part of the zoo will open.

# Morning after sleeping (NIGHT-003)
night-morning-kiga = morning
night-morning-klasse1 = Good morning! The sun is shining.
night-morning-klasse2 = Good morning! You slept well. A new day at the zoo begins.
night-morning-klasse3 = Good morning! The sun is shining, the birds are singing, and the animals in their enclosures are already awake. A new day at the zoo begins. Let's see what there is to do today!

## Burglar event (GAME-EVENTS event 1)

# Cut-in when the burglars are seen (GAME-EVENTS rules 2, 5)
event-burglar-start-kiga = burglars
event-burglar-start-klasse1 = Shh! Two burglars are here!
event-burglar-start-klasse2 = Two sneaky burglars have crept into the zoo and taken a food box. Follow their footprints!
event-burglar-start-klasse3 = Did you hear that? Two clumsy burglars have climbed over the wall and taken a food box. Follow their footprints and shine your lantern on them before they disappear again!

# Dropped note, level 1 (hideout between the west wall and the pond)
event-burglar-note-level_1-kiga = wall
event-burglar-note-level_1-klasse1 = We wait at the wall. Behind the pond.
event-burglar-note-level_1-klasse2 = Meeting point: at the big wall, just behind the pond with the water lilies.
event-burglar-note-level_1-klasse3 = Hi pal! We'll meet tonight at the big zoo wall. Walk past the pond with the frogs, and you'll find us behind the reeds. Bring the sack!

# Dropped note, level 2 (hideout between the elephant enclosure and the east wall)
event-burglar-note-level_2-kiga = elephant
event-burglar-note-level_2-klasse1 = We wait by the elephants. At the wall.
event-burglar-note-level_2-klasse2 = Meeting point: behind the elephants' enclosure, right next to the wall.
event-burglar-note-level_2-klasse3 = Hi pal! We are hiding behind the big enclosure with the grey giants. Nobody can see us there by the zoo wall. Be quiet, or they will trumpet!

# Dropped note, level 3 (hideout between the monkey enclosure and the north wall)
event-burglar-note-level_3-kiga = monkeys
event-burglar-note-level_3-klasse1 = We wait by the monkeys. At the wall.
event-burglar-note-level_3-klasse2 = Meeting point: behind the monkey enclosure, right up by the wall.
event-burglar-note-level_3-klasse3 = Hi pal! We are waiting behind the enclosure where it screeches and climbs so loudly during the day. Our hideout is right at the back by the zoo wall. Make sure nobody sees you!

# Burglars caught in time (EVT-003)
event-burglar-caught-kiga = police
event-burglar-caught-klasse1 = Caught! The police are coming.
event-burglar-caught-klasse2 = Caught! The burglars get a fright, and the police take them away. The food box is back.
event-burglar-caught-klasse3 = Caught! In the light of your lantern the two burglars freeze on the spot. The police arrive with flashing blue lights and take them away. The food box is back, and all the animals sleep on peacefully.

# Time window over (EVT-004; GAME-EVENTS rule 7)
event-burglar-late-kiga = police
event-burglar-late-klasse1 = The police caught them anyway!
event-burglar-late-klasse2 = The burglars escaped over the wall. But the police caught them anyway! The food box is at the entrance.
event-burglar-late-klasse3 = The two burglars quickly climbed over the wall. But the police were already waiting outside and caught them anyway! They dropped the food box; it is now at the zoo entrance.
